# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_derived_publish_failures_total Derived-event publishes that did not get a positive acknowledgement, by outcome: unknown (a timeout: the event may have been stored) or failed (the broker refused it). Each defers its checkpoint and is retried with the same bytes and broker dedup id, so a stored one is not stored twice.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_derived_publish_failures_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_derived_publish_failures_total{outcome="failed"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_derived_publish_failures_total{outcome="unknown"} 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_derived_publish_lane_waits_total Detections that waited for an earlier detection of the same device (or correlation anchor) to be acknowledged before they could be sent, with derivedPublishing.maxInFlight above 1. A high share of all published detections means a few busy series, which a wider window cannot overlap.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_derived_publish_lane_waits_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_derived_publish_lane_waits_total 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_derived_publish_outstanding Derived events sent and waiting for the broker's acknowledgement right now (bounded by derivedPublishing.maxInFlight). Zero between checkpoints.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_derived_publish_outstanding gauge
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_derived_publish_outstanding 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_derived_publish_outstanding_bytes Payload bytes of those derived events (bounded by derivedPublishing.maxBufferedBytes, except that a single larger event is sent on its own).
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_derived_publish_outstanding_bytes gauge
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_derived_publish_outstanding_bytes 0
