devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_fanout_events_total 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_guard_prime_events_total Events read from the stream to prime the duplicate-event guard, summed over term builds.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_guard_prime_events_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_guard_prime_events_total 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_guard_prime_partial_total Term builds whose priming found the stream no longer reaching back the guard's whole retention (the oldest message is newer than the retention before the restored position and is not the first ever written). A duplicate of an event older than that is applied twice. Non-zero means stream retention is shorter than the redelivery span.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_guard_prime_partial_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_guard_prime_partial_total 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_guard_prime_seconds Wall-clock seconds the last term build spent reading the stream to prime the duplicate-event guard. Zero until a build primed one. It is the part of a leader change that grows with the event rate.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_guard_prime_seconds gauge
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_guard_prime_seconds 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_idle_advances_total Wall-clock idle advances that produced at least one detection.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_idle_advances_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_idle_advances_total 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_idle_detections_total Detections produced by wall-clock idle advance (absence/duration/session firing on silence).
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_idle_detections_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_idle_detections_total 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_is_leader 1 while this replica holds the DETECT partition lease, from acquisition rather than from the end of the term build.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_is_leader gauge
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_is_leader 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_late_samples_total Samples that arrived too far behind the watermark to be used, counted once per rule that declined them: after their own trailing window had passed it (Repeating, SlidingAgg, Correlation), or, for a Duration rule, a matching reading more than the rule's hold behind it or a non-matching reading from inside the run of an alarm already raised, older than the raise. A store-and-forward device uploading buffered readings is the usual cause; a sustained non-zero rate means those rules are evaluating less than the device sent.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_late_samples_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_late_samples_total 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live 1 while this replica is consuming inside a held leadership term; 0 while standing by OR while building a term it has already acquired.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live gauge
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live_gap_fills_total Times live consumption met a message whose stream sequence was more than one past the engine's and read the missing range from the stream, by outcome: filled (the range was read and held messages), absent_only (the stream held none of it: purged or evicted), failed (an attempt to read the range did not complete; live consumption parks and the attempt repeats every tick, so a sustained outage counts every attempt, not once).
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live_gap_fills_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live_gap_fills_total{outcome="absent_only"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live_gap_fills_total{outcome="failed"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live_gap_fills_total{outcome="filled"} 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live_gap_sequences_total Stream sequences inside live gap fills, by outcome: applied (a message the broker had counted as delivered that never reached the loop, now applied), absent (not in the stream: purged or evicted), skipped (read back unprocessable, and recorded as handled without applying anything). A non-zero applied rate means deliveries are being lost between the broker and this loop.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live_gap_sequences_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live_gap_sequences_total{outcome="absent"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live_gap_sequences_total{outcome="applied"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live_gap_sequences_total{outcome="skipped"} 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live_keys Total live keyed window/timer state entries across all tenants (the per-tenant state-budget aggregate).
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live_keys gauge
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_live_keys 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_heartbeat_timestamp_seconds Unix time of the last pass of the DETECT single-writer loop, refreshed at least once per tick while a term is live. Stale while detect_is_leader and detect_live read 1 means the loop is hung inside a call.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_heartbeat_timestamp_seconds gauge
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_heartbeat_timestamp_seconds 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_seconds_total Wall-clock seconds the live detection loop has spent in each phase, by phase: fetch_wait (idle, waiting for the next message or tick), decode, plan (rule fan-out), apply (the engine), publish (a checkpoint handing detections to the broker), save (a checkpoint committing the snapshot), ack, gapfill (reading missed sequences), control (rule and roster updates, purges, ticker housekeeping), parked (live messages switched off behind an uncommitted idle advance or an unreadable gap), probe (the ticker's broker backlog round trips). The phases partition the loop's time, so a phase's rate is its share of wall time and the non-wait phases summing to 1 means the loop is saturated.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_seconds_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_seconds_total{phase="ack"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_seconds_total{phase="apply"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_seconds_total{phase="control"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_seconds_total{phase="decode"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_seconds_total{phase="fetch_wait"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_seconds_total{phase="gapfill"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_seconds_total{phase="parked"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_seconds_total{phase="plan"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_seconds_total{phase="probe"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_seconds_total{phase="publish"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_loop_seconds_total{phase="save"} 0
