# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_oldest_pending_seconds Age of the oldest rule-health update not yet written: how stale the console's fire counts may be. Normally under the flush interval plus one write.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_oldest_pending_seconds gauge
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_oldest_pending_seconds 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_pending_bytes Accounted memory of the pending rule-health updates, across the active, detached and in-flight sets (bounded by ruleHealth.maxPendingBytes).
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_pending_bytes gauge
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_pending_bytes 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_pending_keys Distinct rules with fire updates not yet written, across the active, detached and in-flight sets (bounded by ruleHealth.maxPendingKeys).
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_pending_keys gauge
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_pending_keys 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_admitted_total Published detections admitted to the rule-health fire counters, to be written in the background.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_admitted_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_admitted_total 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_coalesced_total Admitted rule-health fire updates that merged into a rule's pending count rather than adding a row to the next write.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_coalesced_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_coalesced_total 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_discarded_total Rule-health fire updates that will never be written, by reason: full (the pending budget was exhausted, so the update was refused at admission), overflow (the rule's pending count is at its ceiling), closed (admitted after the leadership term ended), write_failed (its batch failed or timed out and was not retried), purged (its tenant was deleted first), shutdown (still pending when the term ended). Detection is unaffected; the console's fire counts are short by this much.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_discarded_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_discarded_total{reason="closed"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_discarded_total{reason="full"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_discarded_total{reason="overflow"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_discarded_total{reason="purged"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_discarded_total{reason="shutdown"} 0
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_discarded_total{reason="write_failed"} 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_written_total Rule-health fire updates committed to the database.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_written_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_updates_written_total 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_write_failures_total Rule-health fire counter batch writes (one tenant's transaction) that failed or timed out and were discarded, not retried. Detection is unaffected (the counters are written off the detection loop), but the console's rule-health counts fall short while this rises; the fires lost are in detect_rule_stat_updates_discarded_total with reason write_failed, and the cause is in the service log.
# TYPE devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_write_failures_total counter
devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_write_failures_total 0
# HELP devicechain_eventprocessing_detect_rule_stat_write_seconds Time each rule-health fire counter batch write (one tenant's transaction, including the tenant-deletion check it makes first) took on the background writer. It is not detection-loop time. Failed writes are included; they are also counted in detect_rule_stat_write_failures_total.
